    "updated_at": "2023-02-15T05:47:14Z",
    "body": "I think it might make specs a bit hard to read, as the prose may look like it's returning a different object every time, but a sneaky bit in the IDL is changing the behaviour.\r\n\r\nI'd rather this feature was delivered via some prose defined in infra, like: \"The <ins>memoized getter steps</ins> for foo return…\"\r\n\r\nThere can be an idl comment for it too, of course.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
